## 1. Introduction

FacultyConnect is a web-based platform that enables faculty members to create, manage, and publish their own professional academic websites from a single centralized system. Each faculty member gets a personal dashboard to manage their academic profile, research, publications, courses, and student interactions — while the platform provides a public-facing website for each faculty member that can be shared with students, colleagues, and the broader academic community.

The platform is built on the principle of **data ownership** — faculty members are never permanently locked into the system. They can export their academic data at any time and migrate to their own independent hosting if they choose. This philosophical commitment to data portability distinguishes FacultyConnect from conventional institutional platforms.

FacultyConnect operates as a multi-tenant system where each faculty member's data is stored independently, with both a shared platform database and optional per-faculty independent databases for detached users. The system includes a comprehensive platform administration console for monitoring, managing, and securing the entire platform.

