## 14. Unique Selling Points

### 1. Data Ownership & Portability
Unlike platforms like ResearchGate or Academia.edu, FacultyConnect guarantees that faculty own their data. They can export everything as a standard SQL dump and migrate to independent hosting at any time. The platform actively facilitates departure rather than preventing it.

### 2. Self-Service Faculty Websites
Each faculty member gets a fully functional, professionally designed personal website without any technical knowledge. The platform handles hosting, database management, file storage, and security — faculty just fill in their information.

### 3. Multi-Page Public Profile
The public profile is split into three purpose-built pages (Home, Academic Profile, Publications) rather than cramming everything into one page. This provides a better experience for different visitor types — students visiting for course info vs. researchers looking for publications.

### 4. Embedded Video Support
Faculty can upload lecture videos directly or embed YouTube videos. The public profile renders these as inline players, not external links. This keeps students on the faculty's page.

### 5. Integrated Migration System
The migration workflow includes email verification, hosting detail collection, admin review with mandatory password confirmation, and automatic independent database creation. This is a complete, functional migration pipeline — not just a download button.

### 6. Automated Threat Detection
Built-in detection for XSS, SQL injection, path traversal, and brute force attacks — running on every request without requiring external security tools.

### 7. Role-Based Admin Console
Four admin roles (Super Admin, Platform Admin, Support, Read-Only) with a documented permission matrix. The admin panel is a complete SaaS-style operations console, not a basic CRUD interface.

### 8. Zero External Dependencies
No JavaScript frameworks, no CSS libraries, no database server, no Redis, no background workers. The entire application runs as a single Python process with SQLite.

### 9. Support Session Capability
Admins can temporarily view the platform as any faculty member for troubleshooting — with full audit logging, reason documentation, and a clear exit mechanism.

### 10. Consistent Content Management Pattern
Every content type (qualifications, publications, courses, etc.) follows the same CRUD + toggle visibility pattern, making the system predictable and easy to extend.

