## 15. Project Limitations

### Current Limitations

**Scalability:**
SQLite is suitable for hundreds to low thousands of faculty members but would need to be replaced with PostgreSQL or MySQL for larger deployments. The single-file architecture (app.py) would benefit from being split into modules for larger teams.

**Real-Time Features:**
There are no real-time notifications, WebSocket connections, or live updates. Message notifications require page refresh. A production system would benefit from Server-Sent Events or WebSockets for instant notifications.

**Email Integration:**
Verification codes are displayed in flash messages (demo mode) rather than actually being sent via email. A production deployment would need SMTP or transactional email service integration (SendGrid, Mailgun, etc.).

**File Storage:**
Files are stored on the local filesystem. A production system should use cloud storage (AWS S3, Google Cloud Storage) for reliability, scalability, and CDN delivery.

**Search:**
Faculty search uses basic SQL LIKE queries. A production system with many faculty members would benefit from full-text search (Elasticsearch, Meilisearch, or SQLite FTS5).

**Testing:**
There are no automated tests (unit tests, integration tests, end-to-end tests). A production system should have comprehensive test coverage.

**API:**
There is no REST API. All interaction is through server-rendered HTML. A mobile app or third-party integrations would require an API layer.

**Caching:**
There is no caching layer (Redis, Memcached). Repeated database queries for the same data could be optimized with caching.

**Rate Limiting:**
Login attempt protection is detection-based (logged as threats) but does not actually block IPs or accounts after repeated failures. A production system should implement actual rate limiting.

**Multi-Admin Support:**
The admin system supports multiple admins but does not have granular per-section permissions implemented in code (only the role column and a documented permission matrix). Full RBAC enforcement would require decorator modifications.

**Video Upload Size:**
While the max upload is set to 100 MB, uploaded video files are served directly from the filesystem. Large video files would benefit from streaming and CDN delivery.

**Backup Automation:**
Backups are manual only. There is no scheduled/automated backup system. A production system should run daily backups automatically.

**Mobile App:**
There is no native mobile application. The web interface is responsive but a dedicated app could provide push notifications and offline access.

**Accessibility:**
The UI follows general accessibility practices but has not been audited against WCAG 2.1 AA standards. Keyboard navigation and screen reader support could be improved.

